Falsifies `designware_ethernet::proofs::a_link_is_decoded_only_from_what_the_registers_say`.

The defect: the link decode forgets that an isolated PHY is electrically cut off from the MAC.
A PHY with the isolate bit set and its link bit up then reads as a working link.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(bmcr & mdio::BMCR_ISO == 0)`, on any control word with the
isolate bit set and a status word with the link bit set.

